-- title:
--   Iwahori U_q-elements times the q-idele lie in qwidehatR^×
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b$ be rationals, let $q,q'$ be primes with $q'\neq q$, and suppose `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q'` holds for the quaternion algebra $\mathbb H=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the ring $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division ring exactly when $q'$ lies in $v$. Let $R\subset\mathbb H$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule which is an Eichler order of level $N$, that is, $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for maximal orders $\Lambda_i$ (each maximal among orders containing it) with $[\Lambda_1:R]=N$, and assume $q\nmid N$. Write $\widehat\Lambda$ for [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14), the additive subgroup of $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A^{f}_{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ an integral finite adele, and $\Lambda^{g}$ for [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31), the $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $\mathbb H$ pulled back from $g\widehat\Lambda g^{-1}$. Let $n$ be a unit of $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A^{f}_{\mathbb Q}$ in `primeHeckeSet R q`: $n\in\widehat R$, $q\,n^{-1}\in\widehat R$, $n^{-1}\notin\widehat R$, $q^{-1}n\notin\widehat R$. Let $h$ be a unit in `uHeckeSet R n q`, i.e. $h$ satisfies the same four conditions for the order $R\cap R^{n}$ in place of $R$, together with $(R^{n})^{h}=R$ and $R^{h}\neq R^{n}$. Then there exists $g$ in [`Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer R`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L26), the group of units stabilising $\widehat R$, with $hn=q\cdot g$ in $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A^{f}_{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   This is the idelic identity underlying the second degeneracy relation $b_*\circ U_q=q\,a_*$ between the Brandt modules of the Eichler orders $R\cap R^{n}$ (level $Nq$) and $R$ (level $N$): multiplication by $hn$ acts on $R$-classes as multiplication by the central rational $q$. It is used in the comparison of the two degeneracy maps on the class-set graph and in the description of the $U_q$-cosets as cosets of the stabiliser of $\widehat R$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_exists_mem_finiteIdeleStabilizer_mul_eq_natCast_smul_of_mem_uHeckeSet.lean

